.TH IMAP4 2
.SH NAME
imap4 \- IMAP4rev1 client over TLS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
include "sys.m";
include "keyring.m";
include "tls12.m";
include "imap4.m";
imap4 := load Imap4 Imap4->PATH;
Client: import imap4;
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Imap4
is an IMAP4rev1 (RFC 3501) client that runs over
.IR tls12 (2),
this tree's verifying TLS 1.2 client \(em never a host command.
It is enough to reach modern servers such as Gmail
.RB ( imap.gmail.com :993).
.PP
.B init
loads and initialises
.IR tls12 (2);
call it once.
.PP
.B connect
dials
.I dialip
(or
.I host
if
.I dialip
is empty) at
.IR port ,
runs the TLS handshake naming
.I host
for SNI and certificate verification, and reads the server greeting.
Because a hosted
.I emu
has no
.B /net/cs
to resolve names, a caller may resolve
.I host
to an address outside
.I emu
and pass it as
.I dialip
while the certificate is still checked for
.IR host .
.PP
The returned
.B Client
carries the TLS session and offers methods, each returning a trailing
error string that is nil on success:
.TP
.B capa
Return the server's
.B CAPABILITY
line.
.TP
.B login
Authenticate with
.I user
and
.I pass
(an app password over TLS).
.TP
.B authxoauth2
Authenticate with SASL XOAUTH2 using
.I user
and a caller-supplied OAuth 2.0 bearer
.I token
(Gmail's preferred mechanism).
.TP
.B mailboxes
Return the
.B LIST
lines matching a reference and pattern.
.TP
.BR select ", " examine
Select a mailbox (read-write, or read-only for
.BR examine )
and return its message count.
.TP
.B status
Return the
.B STATUS
line for the given items (e.g.\&
.BR "MESSAGES UNSEEN" )
without selecting the mailbox.
.TP
.B fetch
Fetch one
.I item
(for example
.B "BODY.PEEK[]"
or
.BR "BODY.PEEK[HEADER]" )
of a message, returning its literal bytes exactly.
.TP
.B search
Return the message numbers matching a
.B SEARCH
.I criteria
in the selected mailbox.
.TP
.B store
Set flags on a message, e.g. item
.B "+FLAGS (\eSeen)"
to mark read or
.B "+FLAGS (\eDeleted)"
to mark for expunge.
.TP
.BR copy ", " expunge
Copy a message to another mailbox;
.B expunge
removes messages flagged
.BR \eDeleted .
.TP
.BR create ", " delete ", " rename
Mailbox (folder) management.
.TP
.B docmd
Send a raw command and collect its untagged and completion responses;
the other methods are built on this.
.TP
.B logout
Log out and close the TLS session.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/lib/imap4.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR upas-fetch (1),
.IR tls12 (2),
.IR smtp (2)
.SH BUGS
No STARTTLS (the connection is TLS from the start).
Authentication is
.B LOGIN
or
.B XOAUTH2
(the caller obtains the OAuth token out of band).
Literal handling covers the forms
.B FETCH
produces, not every server response.
UID-based variants of
.B search
and
.B fetch
are not exposed.
